# Agent Use

Repository agents live only in `.cursor/agents/`. Before naming or delegating to
one, verify that its definition exists there and that its declared tools fit
the task. Do not reference global, provider-mirror, or phantom agents.

- Use planning support for large or ambiguous work.
- Use architecture support for consequential boundary decisions.
- Review substantive code changes with evidence.
- Use security review for changes involving untrusted input, gateway routes,
  stream validation, browser storage, or exports.
- Use final-QA guidance when the implementation reaches the risk-based
  validation phase.

Parallelize independent investigations when it reduces latency, but keep one
owner responsible for reconciling findings against the canonical project
contract.
